From: Nikita Maslo <nikitamalco203@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 May 2025 16:22:00 +0300
Subject: arm64: dts: rockchip: overlay: build rk3568-napi2-lvds.dtbo

The NAPI2 (RK3568) LVDS panel overlay source is delivered into
arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/overlay/ by the "overlay-directories" entry in
patch/kernel/rk35xx-vendor-6.1/0000.patching_config.yaml, which only copies
files - it deliberately ships no Makefile of its own, because doing so would
overwrite this kernel's ~300-entry overlay Makefile.

So the build entry has to be patched in. It is added as a fresh "+=" block
rather than by extending the last continued line, to keep the hunk small and
avoid a backslash conflict whenever upstream appends new overlays. It must
stay above "always-y := $(dtbo-y)", which expands immediately.

Note this is unconditional for every rk35xx vendor board (kernel patch dirs
have no board_${BOARD} scoping - BOARD is not passed to the patcher, see
lib/functions/compilation/kernel-patching.sh:31). The cost is one extra
~3 KB .dtbo in the linux-dtb package of unrelated rk35xx boards.

Signed-off-by: Nikita Maslo <nikitamalco203@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/overlay/Makefile | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/overlay/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/overlay/Makefile
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/overlay/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/overlay/Makefile
@@ -349,6 +349,13 @@
 	recomputer-rk3588-devkit-halow-wifi.dtbo \
 	recomputer-rk3588-devkit-raspi-7inch-touchscreen.dtbo
 
+# Armbian: NAPI2 (RK3568) board overlay. The .dts source is dropped into this directory by
+# patch/kernel/rk35xx-vendor-6.1/overlay/ via 'overlay-directories' in 0000.patching_config.yaml;
+# only this Makefile entry has to be patched in. Keep it above 'always-y :=' below, which
+# expands $(dtbo-y) immediately.
+dtbo-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += \
+	rk3568-napi2-lvds.dtbo
+
 dtbotxt-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += \
 	README.rockchip-overlays
 
-- 
Armbian

